# Systematic Workflow Debugging Protocol

When the user asks to fix bugs or optimize a workflow step-by-step, follow this strict operational pipeline. Do not jump ahead.

## 1. Discovery Phase

- Inspect the relevant files in the targeted microservice (`/backend` or `/frontend-nextjs`).
- If applicable, check `docker-compose.yml` or `schema.sql` to understand data shapes and environment variables.
- Present the user with a concise summary of the bug and your proposed line-by-line fix.

## 2. Execution & Review

- Fix exactly ONE isolated bug at a time.
- Do not modify unrelated files in the same turn.
- After applying a fix, explicitly ask the user to verify the changes or run the local test command before moving to the next item.

## 3. The Live Checklist

At the end of EVERY response, output a clean markdown checklist showing the progress of the debugging session.

Example:

- [x] Step 1: Fix backend CORS issue in `cors.json`
- [/] Step 2: Fix Next.js API route data fetching (Current Step)
- [ ] Step 3: Verify Docker container communication
